IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa22-part31-ch2.l4: Part 31, Chapter 2 (Property of dissolved company) of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom),
-- ss 1012 to 1023 (lines 14198-14286 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are copied from it by a
-- script and checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the rule.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "if" / "where" / "unless" / "until" /
--               "within" condition that fails, a flat negative). Each such branch carries
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording). Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Facts a witness can state, and judgments the text hands to the court, are BOOLEAN inputs. Where a section says "as the
-- case may be" (the Crown, the Duchy of Lancaster or the Duke of Cornwall) the case is an input: which of them is
-- entitled is not decided in the sources. Days and months: NOTES.md, fork F1.

§ `Part 31 -- Dissolution and restoration to the register`

§§ `Chapter 2 -- Property of dissolved company`

§§§ `Property vesting as bona vacantia`

-- ---- s 1012: Property of dissolved company to be bona vacantia ----------------------------------------------

-- The three that may take bona vacantia. "As the case may be" is not decided here: an input.
-- src:14202 | (a) accordingly belong to the Crown, or to the Duchy of Lancaster or to the Duke of Cornwall for the time being (as the case may be), and
@ref s 1012(1)(a) Property of dissolved company to be bona vacantia (src:14202)
DECLARE `s 1012(1)(a) owner of bona vacantia` IS ONE OF
    `s 1012(1)(a) the Crown`
    `s 1012(1)(a) the Duchy of Lancaster`
    `s 1012(1)(a) the Duke of Cornwall`

-- (1) When a company is dissolved, all property and rights whatsoever vested in or held on trust for the company
-- immediately before its dissolution (including leasehold property, but not including property held by the company
-- on trust for another person) are deemed to be bona vacantia.
-- src:14201 | (1) When a company is dissolved, all property and rights whatsoever vested in or held on trust for the company immediately before its dissolution (including leasehold property, but not including property held by the company on trust for another person) are deemed to be bona vacantia and—
-- src:14202 | (a) accordingly belong to the Crown, or to the Duchy of Lancaster or to the Duke of Cornwall for the time being (as the case may be), and
-- src:14203 | (b) vest and may be dealt with in the same manner as other bona vacantia accruing to the Crown, to the Duchy of Lancaster or to the Duke of Cornwall.
@ref s 1012(1) Property of dissolved company to be bona vacantia (src:14201-14203)
GIVEN `the company is dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property or right was vested in or held on trust for the company immediately before its dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is held by the company on trust for another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1012(1) the property or right is deemed to be bona vacantia` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is dissolved`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a company is dissolved" (the company is not dissolved: "When" counts as "where", ruled 2026-11-05)
    ELSE IF NOT (`the property or right was vested in or held on trust for the company immediately before its dissolution`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "vested in or held on trust for the company immediately before its dissolution"
         ELSE IF `the property is held by the company on trust for another person`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not including property held by the company on trust for another person"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (1)(a) The property accordingly belongs to the Crown, or to the Duchy of Lancaster or to the Duke of Cornwall for the
-- time being (as the case may be). The "case" is an input.
@ref s 1012(1)(a) Property of dissolved company to be bona vacantia (src:14202)
GIVEN `s 1012(1) the property or right is deemed to be bona vacantia` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the one of them to which bona vacantia accrues in the case` IS A `s 1012(1)(a) owner of bona vacantia`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1012(1)(a) owner of bona vacantia`
`s 1012(1)(a) the owner to whom the property belongs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1012(1) the property or right is deemed to be bona vacantia`
    WHEN JUST deemed THEN
        IF deemed
        THEN JUST `the one of them to which bona vacantia accrues in the case`
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "accordingly belong to the Crown, or to the Duchy of Lancaster or to the Duke of Cornwall"; the property is not deemed bona vacantia, and the text says nothing of whom it then belongs to
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the property is deemed bona vacantia is not known

-- (1)(b) The property vests and may be dealt with in the same manner as other bona vacantia accruing to the Crown, the
-- Duchy of Lancaster or the Duke of Cornwall.
-- src:14203 | (b) vest and may be dealt with in the same manner as other bona vacantia accruing to the Crown, to the Duchy of Lancaster or to the Duke of Cornwall.
@ref s 1012(1)(b) Property of dissolved company to be bona vacantia (src:14203)
GIVEN `s 1012(1) the property or right is deemed to be bona vacantia` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1012(1)(b) the property vests and may be dealt with in the same manner as other bona vacantia` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1012(1) the property or right is deemed to be bona vacantia`
    WHEN JUST deemed THEN
        IF deemed
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "vest and may be dealt with in the same manner as other bona vacantia"; the property is not deemed bona vacantia
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the property is deemed bona vacantia is not known

-- (2) Subsection (1) has effect subject to the possible restoration of the company to the register under Chapter 3
-- (see section 1034). Once the company is restored, section 1034 governs what becomes of property that vested.
-- src:14204 | (2) Subsection (1) has effect subject to the possible restoration of the company to the register under Chapter 3 (see section 1034).
@ref s 1012(2) Property of dissolved company to be bona vacantia (src:14204)
GIVEN `the company has been restored to the register under Chapter 3 of Part 31` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1012(2) the effect of subsection (1) is subject to the restoration of the company to the register` MEANS
    IF `the company has been restored to the register under Chapter 3 of Part 31`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the possible restoration of the company to the register under Chapter 3"; no restoration has happened, so the qualification is not engaged

-- ---- s 1013: Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia --------------------------------------------

-- (1) and (8) The Crown representative: the Treasury Solicitor, or in relation to property in Scotland the Queen's and
-- Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer; for property vested in the Duchy of Lancaster the Solicitor to that Duchy; for property
-- vested in the Duke of Cornwall the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall.
-- src:14206 | (1) Where property vests in the Crown under section 1012, the Crown's title to it under that section may be disclaimed by a notice signed by the Crown representative, that is to say the Treasury Solicitor, or, in relation to property in Scotland, the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer.
@ref s 1013(1) Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia (src:14206)
DECLARE `s 1013(1) Crown representative` IS ONE OF
    `s 1013(1) the Treasury Solicitor`
    `s 1013(1) the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer`
    `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Lancaster`
    `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall`

-- src:14215 | (8) This section applies to property vested in the Duchy of Lancaster or the Duke of Cornwall under section 1012 as if for references to the Crown and the Crown representative there were respectively substituted references to the Duchy of Lancaster and to the Solicitor to that Duchy, or to the Duke of Cornwall and to the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall, as the case may be.
@ref s 1013(8) Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia (src:14215)
GIVEN `the owner of the property under section 1012` IS A `s 1012(1)(a) owner of bona vacantia`
      `the property is in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1013(1) Crown representative`
`s 1013(1) the Crown representative for the property` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the owner of the property under section 1012`
    WHEN `s 1012(1)(a) the Crown` THEN
        IF `the property is in Scotland`
        THEN `s 1013(1) the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer`
        ELSE `s 1013(1) the Treasury Solicitor`
    WHEN `s 1012(1)(a) the Duchy of Lancaster` THEN `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Lancaster`
    WHEN `s 1012(1)(a) the Duke of Cornwall` THEN `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall`

-- (1) Where property vests in the Crown under section 1012, the Crown's title to it may be disclaimed by a notice
-- signed by the Crown representative.
-- src:14206 | (1) Where property vests in the Crown under section 1012, the Crown's title to it under that section may be disclaimed by a notice signed by the Crown representative, that is to say the Treasury Solicitor, or, in relation to property in Scotland, the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer.
@ref s 1013(1) Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia (src:14206)
GIVEN `the property vests in the Crown under section 1012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of disclaimer is signed by the Crown representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1013(1) the Crown's title to the property may be disclaimed by the notice` MEANS
    IF `the property vests in the Crown under section 1012` AND `the notice of disclaimer is signed by the Crown representative`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Crown's title to it under that section may be disclaimed by a notice signed by the Crown representative"; a notice signed by anyone else is not mentioned

-- (2) The right to execute a notice of disclaimer may be waived by or on behalf of the Crown either expressly or by
-- taking possession.
-- src:14207 | (2) The right to execute a notice of disclaimer under this section may be waived by or on behalf of the Crown either expressly or by taking possession.
@ref s 1013(2) Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia (src:14207)
GIVEN `the right has been waived by or on behalf of the Crown expressly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right has been waived by or on behalf of the Crown by taking possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1013(2) the right to execute a notice of disclaimer has been waived` MEANS
    IF `the right has been waived by or on behalf of the Crown expressly` OR `the right has been waived by or on behalf of the Crown by taking possession`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be waived by or on behalf of the Crown either expressly or by taking possession"; no other mode is mentioned, and no "only" closes the two

-- (3) A notice of disclaimer must be executed within three years after (a) the date on which the fact that the property
-- may have vested in the Crown first comes to the notice of the Crown representative, or (b) if ownership of the
-- property is not established at that date, the end of the period reasonably necessary for the Crown representative to
-- establish the ownership of the property.
-- src:14208 | (3) A notice of disclaimer must be executed within three years after—
-- src:14209 | (a) the date on which the fact that the property may have vested in the Crown under section 1012 first comes to the notice of the Crown representative, or
-- src:14210 | (b) if ownership of the property is not established at that date, the end of the period reasonably necessary for the Crown representative to establish the ownership of the property.
@ref s 1013(3) Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia (src:14208-14210)
GIVEN `the date on which the fact that the property may have vested in the Crown first comes to the notice of the Crown representative` IS A DATE
      `ownership of the property is established at that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the end of the period reasonably necessary for the Crown representative to establish the ownership of the property, if it was not established at that date` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 1013(3) the last day for executing the notice of disclaimer` MEANS
    IF `ownership of the property is established at that date`
    THEN JUST (`add years` `the date on which the fact that the property may have vested in the Crown first comes to the notice of the Crown representative` 3)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the end of the period reasonably necessary for the Crown representative to establish the ownership of the property, if it was not established at that date`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the end of the period reasonably necessary for the Crown representative to establish the ownership" is a judgment of reasonableness not given
         WHEN JUST endOfPeriod THEN JUST (`add years` endOfPeriod 3)

-- (4) If an application in writing is made to the Crown representative by a person interested in the property requiring
-- him to decide whether he will or will not disclaim, any notice of disclaimer must be executed within twelve months
-- after the making of the application or such further period as may be allowed by the court.
-- src:14211 | (4) If an application in writing is made to the Crown representative by a person interested in the property requiring him to decide whether he will or will not disclaim, any notice of disclaimer must be executed within twelve months after the making of the application or such further period as may be allowed by the court.
@ref s 1013(4) Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia (src:14211)
GIVEN `the date on which the application in writing was made to the Crown representative` IS A DATE
      `the date to which the court allowed a further period, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1013(4) the last day for executing the notice of disclaimer after an application` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date to which the court allowed a further period, if it did`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add months` `the date on which the application in writing was made to the Crown representative` 12
    WHEN JUST further THEN
        IF further GREATER THAN `add months` `the date on which the application in writing was made to the Crown representative` 12
        THEN further
        ELSE `add months` `the date on which the application in writing was made to the Crown representative` 12

-- (5) A notice of disclaimer is of no effect if it is shown to have been executed after the end of the period
-- specified by subsection (3) or (4).
-- src:14212 | (5) A notice of disclaimer under this section is of no effect if it is shown to have been executed after the end of the period specified by subsection (3) or (4).
@ref s 1013(5) Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia (src:14212)
GIVEN `the date the notice of disclaimer was executed` IS A DATE
      `s 1013(3) the last day for executing the notice of disclaimer` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `s 1013(4) the last day for executing the notice of disclaimer after an application, if an application in writing was made` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1013(5) the notice of disclaimer is of no effect` MEANS
    IF `s 1013(4) the last day for executing the notice of disclaimer after an application, if an application in writing was made` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN CONSIDER `s 1013(3) the last day for executing the notice of disclaimer`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the end of the period under subsection (3) is not known
         WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
             IF `the date the notice of disclaimer was executed` GREATER THAN lastDay
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is of no effect if it is shown to have been executed after the end of the period specified by subsection (3) or (4)" (executed within the period)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1013(4) the last day for executing the notice of disclaimer after an application, if an application in writing was made`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): not reachable
         WHEN JUST lastDayAfterApplication THEN
             IF `the date the notice of disclaimer was executed` GREATER THAN lastDayAfterApplication
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE CONSIDER `s 1013(3) the last day for executing the notice of disclaimer`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the end of the period under subsection (3) is not known
                  WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
                      IF `the date the notice of disclaimer was executed` GREATER THAN lastDay
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is of no effect if it is shown to have been executed after the end of the period specified by subsection (3) or (4)" (executed within both periods)

-- (6) A notice of disclaimer must be delivered to the registrar and retained and registered by him. The duty is the
-- Crown representative's and the registrar's: it is encoded for what it decides, with no seat for an official.
-- src:14213 | (6) A notice of disclaimer under this section must be delivered to the registrar and retained and registered by him.
@ref s 1013(6) Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia (src:14213)
GIVEN `a notice of disclaimer has been executed under section 1013` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1013(6) the notice must be delivered to the registrar and retained and registered by him` MEANS
    IF `a notice of disclaimer has been executed under section 1013`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "A notice of disclaimer under this section must be delivered to the registrar"; with no notice executed the subsection says nothing

-- (7) Copies of the notice must be published in the Gazette and sent to any persons who have given the Crown
-- representative notice that they claim to be interested in the property.
-- src:14214 | (7) Copies of it must be published in the Gazette and sent to any persons who have given the Crown representative notice that they claim to be interested in the property.
@ref s 1013(7) Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia (src:14214)
GIVEN `a notice of disclaimer has been executed under section 1013` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1013(7) copies of the notice must be published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `a notice of disclaimer has been executed under section 1013`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Copies of it must be published in the Gazette"; with no notice executed the subsection says nothing

@ref s 1013(7) Crown disclaimer of property vesting as bona vacantia (src:14214)
GIVEN `a notice of disclaimer has been executed under section 1013` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has given the Crown representative notice that the person claims to be interested in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1013(7) a copy of the notice must be sent to the person` MEANS
    IF `a notice of disclaimer has been executed under section 1013` AND `the person has given the Crown representative notice that the person claims to be interested in the property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "sent to any persons who have given the Crown representative notice that they claim to be interested in the property"; a person who has not given such notice is not mentioned

-- (8) Section 1013 applies to property vested in the Duchy of Lancaster or the Duke of Cornwall as if for references to
-- the Crown and the Crown representative there were substituted the Duchy and its Solicitor, or the Duke and the
-- Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall (the Crown representative function above is the substitution).

-- ---- s 1014: Effect of Crown disclaimer ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) Where notice of disclaimer is executed under section 1013 as respects any property, that property is deemed not
-- to have vested in the Crown under section 1012. A notice that section 1013(5) makes of no effect has no effect here
-- either (NOTES.md, fork F9).
-- src:14217 | (1) Where notice of disclaimer is executed under section 1013 as respects any property, that property is deemed not to have vested in the Crown under section 1012.
@ref s 1014(1) Effect of Crown disclaimer (src:14217)
GIVEN `notice of disclaimer is executed under section 1013 as respects the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1013(5) the notice of disclaimer is of no effect` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1014(1) the property is deemed not to have vested in the Crown under section 1012` MEANS
    IF NOT (`notice of disclaimer is executed under section 1013 as respects the property`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where notice of disclaimer is executed under section 1013 as respects any property" (no notice is executed)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1013(5) the notice of disclaimer is of no effect`
         WHEN JUST voidNotice THEN
             IF voidNotice
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice of disclaimer under this section is of no effect if it is shown to have been executed after the end of the period" (section 1013(5))
             ELSE JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 1013(5) makes the notice of no effect is not known

-- (2) Sections 1015 to 1019 apply in relation to property in England and Wales or Northern Ireland; sections 1020 to
-- 1022 apply in relation to property in Scotland.
-- src:14218 | (2) The following sections contain provisions as to the effect of the Crown disclaimer—
-- src:14219 | sections 1015 to 1019 apply in relation to property in England and Wales or Northern Ireland;
-- src:14220 | sections 1020 to 1022 apply in relation to property in Scotland.
@ref s 1014(2) Effect of Crown disclaimer (src:14218-14220)
DECLARE `s 1014(2) sections providing for the effect of the disclaimer` IS ONE OF
    `s 1014(2) sections 1015 to 1019 (property in England and Wales or Northern Ireland)`
    `s 1014(2) sections 1020 to 1022 (property in Scotland)`
    `s 1014(2) neither set applies (property outside the three)`

@ref s 1014(2) Effect of Crown disclaimer (src:14218-14220)
GIVEN `the property is in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1014(2) sections providing for the effect of the disclaimer`
`s 1014(2) the sections that apply to the property` MEANS
    IF `the property is in England and Wales or Northern Ireland`
    THEN `s 1014(2) sections 1015 to 1019 (property in England and Wales or Northern Ireland)`
    ELSE IF `the property is in Scotland`
         THEN `s 1014(2) sections 1020 to 1022 (property in Scotland)`
         ELSE `s 1014(2) neither set applies (property outside the three)`

§§§ `Effect of Crown disclaimer: England and Wales and Northern Ireland`

-- ---- s 1015: General effect of disclaimer ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) The Crown's disclaimer operates so as to terminate, as from the date of the disclaimer, the rights, interests
-- and liabilities of the company in or in respect of the property disclaimed.
-- src:14223 | (1) The Crown's disclaimer operates so as to terminate, as from the date of the disclaimer, the rights, interests and liabilities of the company in or in respect of the property disclaimed.
@ref s 1015(1) General effect of disclaimer (src:14223)
GIVEN `the date of the disclaimer` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1015(1) the rights, interests and liabilities of the company in or in respect of the property are terminated` MEANS
    IF `the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date of the disclaimer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "terminate, as from the date of the disclaimer, the rights, interests and liabilities of the company" (the date asked about is before the disclaimer)

-- (2) It does not, except so far as is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company from any liability, affect
-- the rights or liabilities of any other person. Where the exception applies the text does not say that other rights
-- are affected, only that the flat negative does not reach that far (fork F10).
-- src:14224 | (2) It does not, except so far as is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company from any liability, affect the rights or liabilities of any other person.
@ref s 1015(2) General effect of disclaimer (src:14224)
GIVEN `the effect on the rights or liabilities of the other person is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company from any liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1015(2) the disclaimer affects the rights or liabilities of the other person` MEANS
    IF `the effect on the rights or liabilities of the other person is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company from any liability`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except so far as is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company from any liability"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It does not, except so far as is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company from any liability, affect the rights or liabilities of any other person"

-- ---- s 1016: Disclaimer of leaseholds -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (3) In section 1016 the "Crown representative" means (a) for property vested in the Duchy of Lancaster, the Solicitor
-- to that Duchy; (b) for property vested in the Duke of Cornwall, the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall; (c) for
-- property in Scotland, the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer; (d) for other property, the Treasury Solicitor.
-- src:14230 | (3) In this section the “Crown representative” means—
-- src:14231 | (a) in relation to property vested in the Duchy of Lancaster, the Solicitor to that Duchy;
-- src:14232 | (b) in relation to property vested in the Duke of Cornwall, the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall;
-- src:14233 | (c) in relation to property in Scotland, the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer;
-- src:14234 | (d) in relation to other property, the Treasury Solicitor.
@ref s 1016(3) Disclaimer of leaseholds (src:14230-14234)
GIVEN `the property is vested in the Duchy of Lancaster` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is vested in the Duke of Cornwall` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1013(1) Crown representative`
`s 1016(3) the Crown representative for the property` MEANS
    IF `the property is vested in the Duchy of Lancaster`
    THEN `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Lancaster`
    ELSE IF `the property is vested in the Duke of Cornwall`
         THEN `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall`
         ELSE IF `the property is in Scotland`
              THEN `s 1013(1) the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer`
              ELSE `s 1013(1) the Treasury Solicitor`

-- (1) The disclaimer of any property of a leasehold character does not take effect unless a copy of the disclaimer has
-- been served (so far as the Crown representative is aware of their addresses) on every person claiming under the
-- company as underlessee or mortgagee, and either (a) no application under section 1017 is made before the end of the
-- period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the last notice under this paragraph was served, or (b) where such
-- an application has been made, the court directs that the disclaimer shall take effect. Encoded as the bar (ruled
-- 2026-11-05 (d)): JUST TRUE while the disclaimer cannot yet take effect, JUST FALSE once the conditions are met.
-- src:14226 | (1) The disclaimer of any property of a leasehold character does not take effect unless a copy of the disclaimer has been served (so far as the Crown representative is aware of their addresses) on every person claiming under the company as underlessee or mortgagee, and either—
-- src:14227 | (a) no application under section 1017 (power of court to make vesting order) is made with respect to that property before the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the last notice under this paragraph was served, or
-- src:14228 | (b) where such an application has been made, the court directs that the disclaimer shall take effect.
@ref s 1016(1) Disclaimer of leaseholds (src:14226-14228)
GIVEN `the property is of a leasehold character` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the disclaimer has been served on every person claiming under the company as underlessee or mortgagee whose address the Crown representative is aware of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the last notice under this paragraph was served` IS A DATE
      `the day on which an application under section 1017 was made, if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the court directs that the disclaimer shall take effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1016(1) the disclaimer of the leasehold property is barred from taking effect` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the property is of a leasehold character`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The disclaimer of any property of a leasehold character"; other property is not mentioned
    ELSE IF NOT (`a copy of the disclaimer has been served on every person claiming under the company as underlessee or mortgagee whose address the Crown representative is aware of`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the day on which an application under section 1017 was made, if one was`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN
                  IF `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `the day on which the last notice under this paragraph was served` PLUS 13
                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not take effect unless ... (a) no application under section 1017 (power of court to make vesting order) is made with respect to that property before the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the last notice under this paragraph was served" (the period has ended and no application was made)
                  ELSE JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST applied THEN
                  IF applied AT MOST `the day on which the last notice under this paragraph was served` PLUS 13
                  THEN IF `the court directs that the disclaimer shall take effect`
                       THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not take effect unless ... (b) where such an application has been made, the court directs that the disclaimer shall take effect"
                       ELSE JUST TRUE
                  ELSE IF `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `the day on which the last notice under this paragraph was served` PLUS 13
                       THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) no application under section 1017 (power of court to make vesting order) is made with respect to that property before the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the last notice under this paragraph was served" (the application came after the period)
                       ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2) Where the court gives a direction under subsection (1)(b) it may also, instead of or in addition to any order it
-- makes under section 1017, make such order as it thinks fit with respect to fixtures, tenant's improvements and
-- other matters arising out of the lease.
-- src:14229 | (2) Where the court gives a direction under subsection (1)(b) it may also, instead of or in addition to any order it makes under section 1017, make such order as it thinks fit with respect to fixtures, tenant's improvements and other matters arising out of the lease.
@ref s 1016(2) Disclaimer of leaseholds (src:14229)
GIVEN `the court gives a direction under section 1016(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1016(2) the court may make such order as it thinks fit with respect to fixtures, tenant's improvements and other matters arising out of the lease` MEANS
    IF `the court gives a direction under section 1016(1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court gives a direction under subsection (1)(b) it may also"

-- ---- s 1017: Power of court to make vesting order --------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) The court may on application by a person who (a) claims an interest in the disclaimed property, or (b) is under a
-- liability in respect of the disclaimed property that is not discharged by the disclaimer, make an order under this
-- section in respect of the property.
-- src:14236 | (1) The court may on application by a person who—
-- src:14237 | (a) claims an interest in the disclaimed property, or
-- src:14238 | (b) is under a liability in respect of the disclaimed property that is not discharged by the disclaimer,
-- src:14239 | make an order under this section in respect of the property.
@ref s 1017(1) Power of court to make vesting order (src:14236-14239)
GIVEN `the person claims an interest in the disclaimed property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is under a liability in respect of the disclaimed property that is not discharged by the disclaimer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1017(1) the court may make a vesting order in respect of the property on the application of the person` MEANS
    IF     `the person claims an interest in the disclaimed property`
       OR  `the person is under a liability in respect of the disclaimed property that is not discharged by the disclaimer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on application by a person who— (a) claims an interest in the disclaimed property, or (b) is under a liability"; no "only" closes the two

-- (2) An order under this section is an order for the vesting of the disclaimed property in, or its delivery to (a) a
-- person entitled to it (or a trustee for such a person), or (b) a person subject to such a liability as is mentioned
-- in subsection (1)(b) (or a trustee for such a person).
-- src:14240 | (2) An order under this section is an order for the vesting of the disclaimed property in, or its delivery to—
-- src:14241 | (a) a person entitled to it (or a trustee for such a person), or
-- src:14242 | (b) a person subject to such a liability as is mentioned in subsection (1)(b) (or a trustee for such a person).
@ref s 1017(2) Power of court to make vesting order (src:14240-14242)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to the property (or is a trustee for such a person)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to such a liability as is mentioned in section 1017(1)(b) (or is a trustee for such a person)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1017(2) an order under section 1017 may vest the disclaimed property in, or deliver it to, the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to the property (or is a trustee for such a person)` OR `the person is subject to such a liability as is mentioned in section 1017(1)(b) (or is a trustee for such a person)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) a person entitled to it ... or (b) a person subject to such a liability"; no "only" closes the two

-- (3) An order under subsection (2)(b) may only be made where it appears to the court that it would be just to do so for
-- the purpose of compensating the person subject to the liability in respect of the disclaimer.
-- src:14243 | (3) An order under subsection (2)(b) may only be made where it appears to the court that it would be just to do so for the purpose of compensating the person subject to the liability in respect of the disclaimer.
@ref s 1017(3) Power of court to make vesting order (src:14243)
GIVEN `it appears to the court that it would be just to make the order for the purpose of compensating the person subject to the liability in respect of the disclaimer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1017(3) an order under subsection (2)(b) may be made` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the court that it would be just to make the order for the purpose of compensating the person subject to the liability in respect of the disclaimer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be made where it appears to the court that it would be just to do so for the purpose of compensating the person subject to the liability"

-- (4) An order under this section may be made on such terms as the court thinks fit.
-- src:14244 | (4) An order under this section may be made on such terms as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 1017(4) Power of court to make vesting order (src:14244)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under section 1017` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1017(4) the order may be made on such terms as the court thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under section 1017`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no order has been made

-- (5) On a vesting order being made under this section, the property comprised in it vests in the person named in that
-- behalf in the order without conveyance, assignment or transfer.
-- src:14245 | (5) On a vesting order being made under this section, the property comprised in it vests in the person named in that behalf in the order without conveyance, assignment or transfer.
@ref s 1017(5) Power of court to make vesting order (src:14245)
GIVEN `a vesting order has been made under section 1017 naming the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1017(5) the property comprised in the order vests in the person named without conveyance, assignment or transfer` MEANS
    IF `a vesting order has been made under section 1017 naming the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On a vesting order being made under this section, the property comprised in it vests in the person named" (no such order has been made: "On" counts as "where", ruled 2026-11-05)

-- ---- s 1018: Protection of persons holding under a lease ---------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) The court must not make an order under section 1017 vesting property of a leasehold nature in a person claiming
-- under the company as underlessee or mortgagee except on terms making that person (a) subject to the same liabilities
-- and obligations as those to which the company was subject under the lease, or (b) if the court thinks fit, subject
-- to the same liabilities and obligations as if the lease had been assigned to him. Encoded as the bar: JUST TRUE while
-- the court is barred, JUST FALSE once the terms are met.
-- src:14247 | (1) The court must not make an order under section 1017 vesting property of a leasehold nature in a person claiming under the company as underlessee or mortgagee except on terms making that person—
-- src:14248 | (a) subject to the same liabilities and obligations as those to which the company was subject under the lease, or
-- src:14249 | (b) if the court thinks fit, subject to the same liabilities and obligations as if the lease had been assigned to him.
@ref s 1018(1) Protection of persons holding under a lease (src:14247-14249)
GIVEN `the property is of a leasehold nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person claims under the company as underlessee or mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is on terms making the person subject to the same liabilities and obligations as those to which the company was subject under the lease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks fit to make the person subject to the same liabilities and obligations as if the lease had been assigned to him, and the order is on those terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1018(1) the court is barred from making the vesting order` MEANS
    IF `the property is of a leasehold nature` AND `the person claims under the company as underlessee or mortgagee`
    THEN IF     `the order is on terms making the person subject to the same liabilities and obligations as those to which the company was subject under the lease`
            OR  `the court thinks fit to make the person subject to the same liabilities and obligations as if the lease had been assigned to him, and the order is on those terms`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not make an order under section 1017 ... except on terms making that person— (a) subject to the same liabilities and obligations ..., or (b) if the court thinks fit, subject to the same liabilities and obligations as if the lease had been assigned to him"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "vesting property of a leasehold nature in a person claiming under the company as underlessee or mortgagee"; other vestings are not mentioned

-- (2) Where the order relates to only part of the property comprised in the lease, subsection (1) applies as if the
-- lease had comprised only the property comprised in the vesting order.
-- src:14250 | (2) Where the order relates to only part of the property comprised in the lease, subsection (1) applies as if the lease had comprised only the property comprised in the vesting order.
@ref s 1018(2) Protection of persons holding under a lease (src:14250)
GIVEN `the order relates to only part of the property comprised in the lease` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1018(2) subsection (1) applies as if the lease had comprised only the property comprised in the vesting order` MEANS
    IF `the order relates to only part of the property comprised in the lease`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the order relates to only part of the property comprised in the lease"; an order for the whole is not mentioned

-- (3) A person claiming under the company as underlessee or mortgagee who declines to accept a vesting order on such
-- terms is excluded from all interest in the property.
-- src:14251 | (3) A person claiming under the company as underlessee or mortgagee who declines to accept a vesting order on such terms is excluded from all interest in the property.
@ref s 1018(3) Protection of persons holding under a lease (src:14251)
GIVEN `the person claims under the company as underlessee or mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person declines to accept a vesting order on such terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1018(3) the person is excluded from all interest in the property` MEANS
    IF `the person claims under the company as underlessee or mortgagee` AND `the person declines to accept a vesting order on such terms`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person claiming under the company as underlessee or mortgagee who declines to accept a vesting order on such terms"; a person who does not decline is not mentioned

-- (4) If there is no person claiming under the company who is willing to accept an order on such terms, the court has
-- power to vest the company's estate and interest in the property in any person who is liable (whether personally or
-- in a representative character, and whether alone or jointly with the company) to perform the lessee's covenants.
-- src:14252 | (4) If there is no person claiming under the company who is willing to accept an order on such terms, the court has power to vest the company's estate and interest in the property in any person who is liable (whether personally or in a representative character, and whether alone or jointly with the company) to perform the lessee's covenants in the lease.
@ref s 1018(4) Protection of persons holding under a lease (src:14252)
GIVEN `there is a person claiming under the company who is willing to accept an order on such terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is liable (whether personally or in a representative character, and whether alone or jointly with the company) to perform the lessee's covenants in the lease` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1018(4) the court has power to vest the company's estate and interest in the property in the person` MEANS
    IF `there is a person claiming under the company who is willing to accept an order on such terms`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If there is no person claiming under the company who is willing to accept an order on such terms" (there is such a person, and the text does not say that the court has no power) (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F24: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    ELSE IF `the person is liable (whether personally or in a representative character, and whether alone or jointly with the company) to perform the lessee's covenants in the lease`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any person who is liable (whether personally or in a representative character, and whether alone or jointly with the company) to perform the lessee's covenants in the lease"; a person not so liable is not mentioned

-- (5) The court may vest that estate and interest in such a person freed and discharged from all estates, incumbrances
-- and interests created by the company.
-- src:14253 | (5) The court may vest that estate and interest in such a person freed and discharged from all estates, incumbrances and interests created by the company.
@ref s 1018(5) Protection of persons holding under a lease (src:14253)
GIVEN `the court vests the estate and interest in a person under section 1018(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1018(5) the court may vest the estate and interest freed and discharged from all estates, incumbrances and interests created by the company` MEANS
    IF `the court vests the estate and interest in a person under section 1018(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may vest that estate and interest in such a person"; a vesting under another provision is not mentioned

-- ---- s 1019: Land subject to rentcharge --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Where in consequence of the disclaimer land that is subject to a rentcharge vests in any person, neither he nor his
-- successors in title are subject to any personal liability in respect of sums becoming due under the rentcharge, except
-- sums becoming due after he, or some person claiming under or through him, has taken possession or control of the land
-- or has entered into occupation of it. The exception takes those sums out of the flat negative (fork F10).
-- src:14255 | Where in consequence of the disclaimer land that is subject to a rentcharge vests in any person, neither he nor his successors in title are subject to any personal liability in respect of sums becoming due under the rentcharge, except sums becoming due after he, or some person claiming under or through him, has taken possession or control of the land or has entered into occupation of it.
@ref s 1019 Land subject to rentcharge (src:14255)
GIVEN `land subject to a rentcharge vests in the person in consequence of the disclaimer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum becomes due after the person, or some person claiming under or through him, has taken possession or control of the land or has entered into occupation of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1019 the person or his successors in title are subject to personal liability for the sum due under the rentcharge` MEANS
    IF NOT (`land subject to a rentcharge vests in the person in consequence of the disclaimer`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where in consequence of the disclaimer land that is subject to a rentcharge vests in any person"
    ELSE IF `the sum becomes due after the person, or some person claiming under or through him, has taken possession or control of the land or has entered into occupation of it`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except sums becoming due after he, or some person claiming under or through him, has taken possession or control of the land or has entered into occupation of it"
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "neither he nor his successors in title are subject to any personal liability in respect of sums becoming due under the rentcharge"

§§§ `Effect of Crown disclaimer: Scotland`

-- ---- s 1020: General effect of disclaimer ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) The Crown's disclaimer operates to determine, as from the date of the disclaimer, the rights, interests and
-- liabilities of the company, and the property of the company, in or in respect of the property disclaimed.
-- src:14258 | (1) The Crown's disclaimer operates to determine, as from the date of the disclaimer, the rights, interests and liabilities of the company, and the property of the company, in or in respect of the property disclaimed.
@ref s 1020(1) General effect of disclaimer (src:14258)
GIVEN `the date of the disclaimer` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1020(1) the rights, interests and liabilities of the company, and the property of the company, in or in respect of the property are determined` MEANS
    IF `the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date of the disclaimer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "operates to determine, as from the date of the disclaimer, the rights, interests and liabilities of the company" (the date asked about is before the disclaimer)

-- (2) It does not (except so far as is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company and its property from
-- liability) affect the rights or liabilities of any other person.
-- src:14259 | (2) It does not (except so far as is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company and its property from liability) affect the rights or liabilities of any other person.
@ref s 1020(2) General effect of disclaimer (src:14259)
GIVEN `the effect on the rights or liabilities of the other person is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company and its property from liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1020(2) the disclaimer affects the rights or liabilities of the other person` MEANS
    IF `the effect on the rights or liabilities of the other person is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company and its property from liability`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except so far as is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company and its property from liability"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It does not (except so far as is necessary for the purpose of releasing the company and its property from liability) affect the rights or liabilities of any other person"

-- ---- s 1021: Power of court to make vesting order ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) The court may, (a) on application by a person who either claims an interest in disclaimed property or is under a
-- liability not discharged by this Act in respect of disclaimed property, and (b) on hearing such persons as it thinks
-- fit, make an order for the vesting of the property in or its delivery to any persons entitled to it, or to whom it
-- may seem just that the property should be delivered by way of compensation for such liability, or a trustee for him.
-- src:14261 | (1) The court may—
-- src:14262 | (a) on application by a person who either claims an interest in disclaimed property or is under a liability not discharged by this Act in respect of disclaimed property, and
-- src:14263 | (b) on hearing such persons as it thinks fit,
-- src:14264 | make an order for the vesting of the property in or its delivery to any persons entitled to it, or to whom it may seem just that the property should be delivered by way of compensation for such liability, or a trustee for him.
@ref s 1021(1) Power of court to make vesting order (src:14261-14264)
GIVEN `the person claims an interest in the disclaimed property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is under a liability not discharged by this Act in respect of the disclaimed property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has heard such persons as it thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1021(1) the court may make a vesting order in respect of the property on the application of the person` MEANS
    IF     (    `the person claims an interest in the disclaimed property`
            OR  `the person is under a liability not discharged by this Act in respect of the disclaimed property`)
       AND `the court has heard such persons as it thinks fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) on application by a person who either claims an interest ... or is under a liability not discharged by this Act ..., and (b) on hearing such persons as it thinks fit"; a case outside the two limbs is not mentioned

-- (2) The order may be made on such terms as the court thinks fit.
-- src:14265 | (2) The order may be made on such terms as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 1021(2) Power of court to make vesting order (src:14265)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under section 1021` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1021(2) the order may be made on such terms as the court thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under section 1021`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no order has been made

-- (3) On a vesting order being made under this section, the property comprised in it vests accordingly in the person
-- named in that behalf in the order, without conveyance or assignation for that purpose.
-- src:14266 | (3) On a vesting order being made under this section, the property comprised in it vests accordingly in the person named in that behalf in the order, without conveyance or assignation for that purpose.
@ref s 1021(3) Power of court to make vesting order (src:14266)
GIVEN `a vesting order has been made under section 1021 naming the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1021(3) the property comprised in the order vests in the person named without conveyance or assignation` MEANS
    IF `a vesting order has been made under section 1021 naming the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On a vesting order being made under this section, the property comprised in it vests accordingly in the person named" (no such order has been made: "On" counts as "where", ruled 2026-11-05)

-- ---- s 1022: Protection of persons holding under a lease --------------------------------------------------------

-- (6) For the purposes of section 1022 a heritable security (a) is duly recorded if it is recorded in the Register of
-- Sasines, and (b) is duly registered if registered in accordance with the Land Registration etc. (Scotland) Act 2012.
-- src:14279 | (6) For the purposes of this section a heritable security—
-- src:14280 | (a) is duly recorded if it is recorded in the Register of Sasines, and
-- src:14281 | (b) is duly registered if registered in accordance with the Land Registration etc. (Scotland) Act 2012 (asp 5).
@ref s 1022(6) Protection of persons holding under a lease (src:14279-14281)
GIVEN `the heritable security is recorded in the Register of Sasines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the heritable security is registered in accordance with the Land Registration etc. (Scotland) Act 2012 (asp 5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1022(6) the heritable security is duly recorded or duly registered` MEANS
    IF `the heritable security is recorded in the Register of Sasines` OR `the heritable security is registered in accordance with the Land Registration etc. (Scotland) Act 2012 (asp 5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a heritable security— (a) is duly recorded if it is recorded in the Register of Sasines, and (b) is duly registered if registered in accordance with the Land Registration etc. (Scotland) Act 2012"

-- (1) and (2) Where the property disclaimed is held under a lease the court must not make a vesting order in favour of a
-- person claiming under the company as sub-lessee or as creditor in a duly registered or recorded heritable security
-- over a lease, except on the following terms: the person must by the order be made subject (a) to the same liabilities
-- and obligations as those to which the company was subject under the lease in respect of the property, or (b) if the
-- court thinks fit, only to the same liabilities and obligations as if the lease had been assigned to him; in either
-- event the liabilities must be as if the lease had comprised only the property comprised in the vesting order.
-- src:14268 | (1) Where the property disclaimed is held under a lease the court must not make a vesting order in favour of a person claiming under the company, whether—
-- src:14269 | (a) as sub-lessee, or
-- src:14270 | (b) as creditor in a duly registered or (as the case may be) recorded heritable security over a lease,
-- src:14271 | except on the following terms.
-- src:14272 | (2) The person must by the order be made subject—
-- src:14273 | (a) to the same liabilities and obligations as those to which the company was subject under the lease in respect of the property, or
-- src:14274 | (b) if the court thinks fit, only to the same liabilities and obligations as if the lease had been assigned to him.
-- src:14275 | In either event (if the case so requires) the liabilities and obligations must be as if the lease had comprised only the property comprised in the vesting order.
@ref s 1022(1) Protection of persons holding under a lease (src:14268-14275)
GIVEN `the property disclaimed is held under a lease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person claims under the company as sub-lessee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1022(6) the heritable security is duly recorded or duly registered` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person claims under the company as creditor in the heritable security over a lease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is on terms making the person subject to the same liabilities and obligations as those to which the company was subject under the lease in respect of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks fit to make the person subject only to the same liabilities and obligations as if the lease had been assigned to him, and the order is on those terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1022(1) the court is barred from making the vesting order in favour of the person` MEANS
    IF     `the property disclaimed is held under a lease`
       AND (   `the person claims under the company as sub-lessee`
            OR (`the person claims under the company as creditor in the heritable security over a lease` AND `s 1022(6) the heritable security is duly recorded or duly registered` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
    THEN IF     `the order is on terms making the person subject to the same liabilities and obligations as those to which the company was subject under the lease in respect of the property`
            OR  `the court thinks fit to make the person subject only to the same liabilities and obligations as if the lease had been assigned to him, and the order is on those terms`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court must not make a vesting order in favour of a person claiming under the company ... except on the following terms"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the property disclaimed is held under a lease the court must not make a vesting order in favour of a person claiming under the company, whether— (a) as sub-lessee, or (b) as creditor in a duly registered or (as the case may be) recorded heritable security over a lease"; other cases are not mentioned

-- (3) A sub-lessee or creditor declining to accept a vesting order on such terms is excluded from all interest in and
-- security over the property.
