      `the company is dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland that is subject to a rentcharge vests by operation of law in the Crown or any other person on the dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1023(1) section 1023 applies` MEANS
    IF `the company is dissolved` AND `land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland that is subject to a rentcharge vests by operation of law in the Crown or any other person on the dissolution`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 1023(3) the person is a company for the purposes of section 1023`
         WHEN JUST isCompany THEN
             IF isCompany
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not a company within the meaning of subsection (3)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where on the dissolution of a company land in England and Wales or Northern Ireland that is subject to a rentcharge vests by operation of law in the Crown or any other person"; no "only" closes the scope

-- (2) Neither the proprietor nor his successors in title are subject to any personal liability in respect of sums
-- becoming due under the rentcharge, except sums becoming due after the proprietor, or some person claiming under or
-- through him, has taken possession or control of the land or has entered into occupation of it.
